# The build context is the repo root; three trees are copied — `spec/rust`,
# `sdk/rust` and `engine/rust` — because `engine/rust` path-depends on the
# other two. Excluding the rest keeps the context small; excluding the target
# directories keeps a host build from being shipped into the image, where its
# absolute paths and host glibc are wrong anyway.
#
# Note `spec/` is NOT excluded wholesale: `spec/rust` holds `stepd-proto`, and
# every crate in the tree depends on it. Its non-Rust parts are markdown, JSON
# fixtures and a virtualenv, all covered by the patterns below.
.git
.github
.claude
docs
reference
**/target
**/*.md
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/node_modules
.env
.env.*
